spu: (vector-type)(e1, ..., en) literals and (vector-type)(scalar) splats

PS3 SPU sources write vector constants as a parenthesised list after a
cast to a vector type, and splats as a cast of one scalar.  GCC parses the
list as a comma expression and rejects the cast of the resulting scalar.

-fparen-vector-literals (C and C++; on by default for SPU, set in
spu-c.c) makes the parser read the parenthesised operand of a cast to a
vector type as a list:
  n >= 2   a vector literal; each element is converted to the element
           type as by a cast; missing elements are zero, extra elements
           are dropped, and either mismatch is warned about
  n == 1   a splat of an arithmetic scalar converted to the element type;
           a vector (or any other) operand is an ordinary cast, postfix
           operators included
A cast to a vector type that is still dependent in a template keeps the
ordinary meaning.

